Notebook[{
Cell[TextData[{
 "We compute electron star profiles and free energy using the equations \
presented in [arXiv:2602.10460]. We tune two core thermodynamic parameters: \
the central temperature and the central chemical potential ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["T", "0"], ",", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "0"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1fa5f36f-2ae9-b14b-bf9e-79a035c89be5"],
 "). From these, we obtain different star profiles and identify the boundary \
thermodynamic parameters ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["T", "\[Infinity]"], ",", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "\[Infinity]"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"d67f6671-e563-4449-a6ed-61f4b67f2eb2"],
 ") following the procedure explained in the paper.\n\nThe program is divided \
into three sections: 1. Computes profiles for a fixed pair of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["T", "0"], ",", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "0"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "895f9988-72f9-1147-9c6a-92b12aa23866"],
 "); 2. Computes profiles by varying ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["T", "0"], ",", 
     SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "0"]}]}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ea0af427-c046-9443-a964-daa7a88dd8c1"],
 ") while keeping the ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[Mu]", "0"], 
    SubscriptBox["T", "0"]], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5ca9b508-2783-624d-be63-353dc7ccc595"],
 " constant; 3. Computes profiles at zero temperature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["T", "0"], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["T", "\[Infinity]"], "=", "0"}]}], ")"}], 
   TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->"202b50d7-e3ae-4148-b14f-0510d798bc8b"],
 ".\n\nParameters\n- Physical (\[Gamma] & mt): Fixed throughout the section \
execution, which can be modified to obtain profiles for different charged \
fluids.\n- Numerical (order): The order of the polynomial expansion around \
r=0. The convergence radius of this expansion determines the initial values \
needed for NDSolve."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9888077316644726`*^9, 3.988807822087675*^9}, {
